cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CalciumImage: Calcium imaging analysis for microfluidic SCN explant culture"
abstract: >-
  An R Shiny pipeline for analyzing calcium imaging data from prairie vole
  suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN) explants cultured on a 3D-printed bubble
  perfusion microfluidic chip. Handles import of raw Calbryte 520 AM
  fluorescence traces, interactive removal of oxygen bubble artifacts,
  one-phase exponential photobleaching correction, and frame-level Wilcoxon
  rank-sum testing with Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Richard
    family-names: Ortiz
    email: rortiz@niu.edu
    affiliation: "Northern Illinois University, Department of Psychology"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1209-9744"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/richard-ortiz/cal.image"
keywords:
  - calcium-imaging
  - suprachiasmatic-nucleus
  - prairie-vole
  - microfluidics
  - photobleaching-correction
  - shiny
  - neuroscience

